{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017jkZbu7J5s1bdgkiozRsbJ","type":"tool_result","content":"858-> Both are legitimate ways to staff a task. Confusing them costs you in exactly one direction: treat interchangeable crew as irreplaceable and you carry unnecessary machinery; treat irreplaceable crew as interchangeable and you lose data.\n859-\n860-### A loop left open on purpose\n861-\n862:You have now been told that a StatefulSet's Pods each get their own persistent storage, and you have not been told how that storage is provisioned, requested, sized, reclaimed, or shared. That is deliberate, and you should know it is deliberate rather than wonder what got skipped.\n863-\n864-The storage half of this — PersistentVolume, PersistentVolumeClaim, StorageClass, access modes, and the provisioning path — is a chapter of its own, and it needs vocabulary this chapter has not built.\n865-\n866-[Omitted long context line]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"31106b91-ec4e-42ac-b7aa-e7d7991f7449","uuid":"9425c19f-f2a5-4fd4-a353-2038e91ef74c","timestamp":"2026-08-25T08:55:59.683Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"858-> Both are legitimate ways to staff a task. Confusing them costs you in exactly one direction: treat interchangeable crew as irreplaceable and you carry unnecessary machinery; treat irreplaceable crew as interchangeable and you lose data.\n859-\n860-### A loop left open on purpose\n861-\n862:You have now been told that a StatefulSet's Pods each get their own persistent storage, and you have not been told how that storage is provisioned, requested, sized, reclaimed, or shared. That is deliberate, and you should know it is deliberate rather than wonder what got skipped.\n863-\n864-The storage half of this — PersistentVolume, PersistentVolumeClaim, StorageClass, access modes, and the provisioning path — is a chapter of its own, and it needs vocabulary this chapter has not built.\n865-\