{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RxXD6onqqHDdzyMe4bRfkQ","type":"tool_result","content":"762:- **B is the most seductive** of the three because a volume feels live in a way an environment variable does not, and in some configurations the projected file content does eventually change on disk. The application still has to be written to notice, though, and a container using a ConfigMap as a `subPath` volume mount will not receive updates at all [source: k8s-docs-volumes-2026-08-23] *[cross-bearing: see Ch 11 — ConfigMap and Secret volumes, and the `subPath` exception]*. Treating \"it's a volume, so it's live\" as a rule will burn you.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"31106b91-ec4e-42ac-b7aa-e7d7991f7449","uuid":"6f5c1a62-f80f-4566-87e6-0bd564fef97d","timestamp":"2026-08-25T08:56:13.057Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"762:- **B is the most seductive** of the three because a volume feels live in a way an environment variable does not, and in some configurations the projected file content does eventually change on disk. The application still has to be written to notice, though, and a container using a ConfigMap as a `subPath` volume mount will not receive updates at all [source: k8s-docs-volumes-2026-08-23] *[cross-bearing: see Ch 11 — ConfigMap and Secret volumes, and the `subPath` exception]*. Treating \"it's a volume, so it's live\" as a rule will burn you.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
