{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011vMaWJRF7KbN3wFTeEGkjZ","type":"tool_result","content":"=== Ch4 PVC ===\n0\n=== Ch6 volumeClaimTemplates / www-web ===\n=== Ch5 projected token ===\n148:    - \"projected-token-volume\"\n775:In Kubernetes v1.22 and later, Kubernetes gets a **short-lived, automatically rotating token** using the TokenRequest API and mounts it as a **projected volume** *[cross-bearing: see Ch 11 — projected volumes]*. Long-lived ServiceAccount token Secrets, the type Chapter 4 listed, don't expire or rotate and are not recommended [source: k8s-docs-service-accounts-2026-08-23]. The type still exists; it's the legacy form [source: k8s-docs-secret-2026-08-23].\n1135:<!-- AUTHOR-REVIEW: budget delta. The Ch 5 outline allocates 21 Practice questions; this revision carries 23. The two additions (Q22, phase + init containers; Q23, multi-container + phase) close the two interleaving gaps the question-quality audit named and are the only realistic way to test `phase-succeeded`, which was previously untested. Offsetting: the 2–3 QoS items the audit anticipated are NOT added, because §8's QoS material is blocked on an unmaterialized snapshot — so chapter total lands at 46 rather than the 46–47 the audit projected. If the 21 budget must hold exactly, the cut candidate identified by the audit is Q17 (three structurally identical distractors, and its correct answer rests on an inferred rather than sourced orthogonality claim — see the author-review in §7). Retrieval rate with 23 items: 8 of 38 Bearings + Practice = 21.1%, above the 20% target the arc outline sets for Chapter 5. -->\n1378:In Kubernetes v1.22 and later, Kubernetes gets a short-lived, automatically rotating token using the TokenRequest API and mounts it as a projected volume; long-lived ServiceAccount token Secrets are not recommended [source: k8s-docs-service-accounts-2026-08-23] [source: k8s-docs-secret-2026-08-23].","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":