{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014dWCXmuEfVUhgH3y2TiSfF","type":"tool_result","content":"25:#--   chapter-01 line 435  -> *[see Ch 6 §3 - StatefulSets and stable identity]*   <-- COLLIDES\n810:That identity is concrete, not conceptual. For a StatefulSet with N replicas, each Pod is assigned an integer ordinal unique across the set — by default, from 0 through N−1 — and each Pod derives its hostname from the StatefulSet's name and its own ordinal. The pattern is `$(statefulset name)-$(ordinal)`, so a three-replica StatefulSet named `web` produces `web-0`, `web-1` and `web-2` [source: k8s-docs-statefulset-2026-08-24].\n874:<!-- AUTHOR-REVIEW: chapter-01 line 435 carries a published cross-bearing reading \"*[see Ch 6 §3 — StatefulSets and stable identity]*\". StatefulSet is §6 in this chapter, and §3 is pinned by chapter-04 line 688 (selectors and ownership), which cannot move. Per the outline's Open Question #1, the recommended fix is a one-token edit in chapter-01: §3 → §6. Not fixable from inside this draft. -->\n1338:B) That each Pod keeps a stable ordinal identity and hostname across rescheduling — carried by the Pod's ordinal and derived name, not by the selector\n1372:[Omitted long matching line]\n1396:[Omitted long matching line]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"31106b91-ec4e-42ac-b7aa-e7d7991f7449","uuid":"11ce59ab-d549-4b06-abac-a8bf10956a05","timestamp":"2026-08-25T08:57:36.767Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"25:#--   chapter-01 line 435  -> *[see Ch 6 §3 - StatefulSets and stable identity]*   <-- COLLIDES\n810:That identity is concrete, not conceptual. For a StatefulSet with N replicas, each Pod is assigned an integer ordinal unique across the set — by default, from 0 through N−1 — and each Pod derives its hostname from the StatefulSet's name and its own ordinal. The pattern is `$(statefulset name)-$(ordinal)`, so a three-replica StatefulSet named `web` produces `web-0`, `web-1` and `web-2` [source: k8s-docs-statefulset-2026-08-24].\n874:<!-- AUTHOR-REVIEW: chapter-01 line 435 carries a published cross-bearing reading \"*[see Ch 6 §3 — StatefulSets and stable identity]*\". StatefulSet is §6 in this chapter, and §3 is pinned by chapter-04 line 688 (selectors and ownership), which cannot move. Per the outline's Open Question #1, the recommended fix is a one-token edit in chapter-01: §3 → §6. Not fixable from inside this draft. -->\n1338:B) That each Pod keeps a stable ordinal identity and hostname across rescheduling — carried by the Pod's ordinal and derived name, not by the selector\n1372:[Omitted long matching line]\n1396:[Omitted long matching line]","numLines":6,"totalLines":6}}
